  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The team has expanded with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Omar Jensen is leading the development phase, which follows the design phase. A larger budget of $2M has been approved by the executive board, with allocations to be discussed on August 1st. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th, and user interface enhancements are planned to commence in October."
